cmney7d83000011oevabeekfi	During the Compiler Design lab viva, one student walked up for her turn.\nAt first, it felt like a normal round of questioning… but it didn’t stay that way for long.\n\nThe questions kept coming.\nFaster. Sharper. Less like guidance, more like pressure stacking up.\n\nYou could see the student trying to hold it together, answering, hesitating, second-guessing… until it got too much. She broke down right there.\n\nAnd in that moment, something felt off.\n\nIt wasn’t just that the questioning continued.\nIt was the energy. Almost like the intensity wasn’t accidental… like there was a certain satisfaction in pushing things to that point.\n\nThe room went quiet after that.\nNot the kind of silence that follows a tough exam… but the kind that makes people look at each other and think, “yeah… that didn’t feel right.” I don’t know how people like this can even be called “TEACHERS “ almost feels like sach people are a shame for the rest who are actually worth the name	Faculty	0	882477c2f5d89ae74f9a315d9e172917e00b98277bed5c095eb2c9e2ed3e328f	2026-03-31 18:26:20.945	2026-04-01 18:26:20.944	f	\N
